          <p>
            The colours are a guide, not a standard. FrogTape uses green for medium and yellow for low adhesion, 3M sells most of its ScotchBlue range in blue whatever the adhesion, and exterior tapes come in several colours. Read the adhesion level and the surface list on the label rather than buying by colour, especially when you are standing in an aisle with a dozen similar rolls.
          </p>

          <p>
            The most common mistake is not using too weak a tape, it is using a medium tape on a surface that needed a low one. A medium tape on fresh paint will usually work, which is why people keep doing it, and then one day it pulls a strip of ceiling paint off with it. If you are unsure, go lower: a low-adhesion tape on a cured surface costs you a little hold, while a medium tape on a soft surface can cost you a repaint.
          </p>
        </div>

