        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy tape by adhesion level and removal window, not by colour or brand. FrogTape Multi-Surface is the best single roll for cured walls and trim, with the sharpest lines on typical textures and a 21-day window. For anything painted in the last week, switch to a delicate tape such as FrogTape Delicate Surface or ScotchBlue Delicate 2080EL, and for anything in the sun, use a UV-rated exterior tape.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then remember that tape is a tool, not a requirement. Burnish the edge, keep the paint thin against it, and pull it while the last coat is still soft. And on textured ceilings, wavy corners and same-day second colours, a good brush and a steady hand will beat any tape on this list.
